    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1351">

                <pb facs="1328" n="1318" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/8–849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Counselor of Embassy in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Nanking</hi><anchor n="41" xml:id="d1351-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-25T16:00:00-04:00">August 25, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1016. Heads mission boards state missionaries in field have full auth make own
                    decisions re evacuation without prior consent hdqrs US. <pb facs="1329" n="1319"
                        xml:id="pg1319"/> If you have knowledge missionaries desiring leave but
                    awaiting consent hdqrs US which not yet forthcoming pls inform Dept names
                    persons and their mission boards and Dept will bring attn boards concerned.
                    (Embtel 1698, Aug 3<anchor n="42" xml:id="d1351-f2"/> and Cantel 862 Aug 1.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1351-f1" n="41" type="source" xml:id="d1351-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Chargé in China as telCan No. 621.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1351-f2" n="42" xml:id="d1351-f2-content">
